            <guid>50057956</guid>
            <pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:36:21 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://uk.finance.yahoo.com/news/french-supermarket-chains-cyberattack-forced-115141288.html">https://uk.finance.yahoo.com/news/french-supermarket-chains-cyberattack-forced-115141288.html</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50057956">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div id="main-content-wrapper">     <article data-testid="article-content-wrapper">        <div data-testid="article-body">   <figure data-testid="article-figure-image"><div> <p><a href="https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/ad468412d2c9c46167646514da916316d51db892f769ec31b1bb6b088d76e191/lightyear_networkapi/resizefit_w960%3Bquality_80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.zenfs.com%2Fen%2Fafp.co.uk%2F49fecac01ece0cd6f086bfbcdae568b5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///ywAAAAAAQABAAACAUwAOw==" alt="" height="511" width="768"></a></p></div> <figcaption><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Intermarche was one of the groups affected (Gabriel BOUYS)<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </figcaption> </figure>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Major French supermarket chains on Monday said they were hit by a cyberattack that caused their refrigerators to shoot up in temperature in hundreds of stores, forcing spoiled food to be thrown away and raising concerns about food security.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Top retailers E. Leclerc, Intermarche and Cooperative U confirmed to AFP they suffered a cyberattack that Cooperative U's chief executive described as "unprecedented".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>            <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->"Food security requires more attention at all levels," said the EU's food and agriculture commissioner Christophe Hansen on X, condemning the attack and saying such "exploitation of food" was now a "reality".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->At least 300 shops of Intermarche or its Netto brand were targeted, along with over 100 Cooperative U outlets, and several E. Leclerc stores, the retailers told AFP in separate statements.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Paris prosecutors confirmed the attack, which reportedly also hit other major chains, and also indicated it had sparked fires.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->BFM TV said hackers "managed to remotely trigger the forced defrosting of the refrigeration systems in numerous stores".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Those branches that were affected will have to "throw away all of the products" that are fresh and frozen, Intermarche told AFP.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Specialist French retail sector news website jebosseengrandedistribution.fr said other retail giants Carrefour Market and Monoprix were affected but the companies have yet to confirm this.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>            <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->E. Leclerc confirmed to AFP "that a cyberattack affected one of its refrigeration equipment suppliers," resulting in "repercussions on the operation of refrigeration systems in several stores".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->A source close to the issue said refrigeration control systems from Danish manufacturer Danfoss were targeted.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Danfoss told AFP in a statement that most of the affected equipment was "legacy" products which "no longer receive software or security updates".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->It said its AK-SM800 and AK-SC355 fridge regulator systems were notably affected, with a version of the former using "outdated firmware". It added that it had long advised supermarkets to update from those models. Danfoss gave no figures of how many systems were affected.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->- Effort to contain the hack -<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->A person close to French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said France's cyber security agency had already identified "a vulnerability in software supplied by a Danish company and has contacted the vendor".<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>             <p><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->"It is liaising with its European counterparts, as other countries may be affected," and is seeking "to identify other French companies involved in order to alert them" and "prevent the spread", the source added.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>  </div> <span> </span> </article>      </div></div>]]></description>
