      <pre>…after <a data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046/hovercard" href="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046"><tt>ebdaf93</tt></a>'s stated 11:10 coverage end; this session's feeds pulled 12:02-12:15 UTC across four passes - the parallel batch died at the 300s mark with 13/45 landed, an --http1.1 -4 browser-UA sequential pass recovered 11 more, a plain browser-UA pass recovered 15 more, and a googlebot-UA pass plus a final plain-UA retry recovered qbitai/solidot/swillison/webkit, 44/45 landed; missed on all attempts: rust - blog.rust-lang.org unreachable, newest stamp carried unchanged from the recordings (Oct 2 standing stale) so no in-window cost; shells this pass: mydrivers 404-1231B, oschina 404-1548B, register 404-204KB, svelte/tailwind/nextjs/vscode 404-pages, nodejs 404-98KB parse-0, anthropic 404-20KB; an unrelated untracked weibo-mss.json sat in the worktree from a concurrent session and is not part of this commit): three adds. (1) An "unprecedented" cyberattack has crippled supermarket refrigeration across Europe: hackers took control of Danfoss-made refrigeration control systems used by French supermarkets Intermarché, Leclerc and Coopérative U and set the automatic defrost function - normally two hours a day - into a continuous forced defrost cycle at 50 degrees C, disrupting deliveries and electronic-shelf-label in-store pricing; Coopérative U president Dominique Schelcher confirmed Monday morning that a cyberattack had been affecting the refrigeration production facilities of several stores in the network since the previous night, calling it extremely serious and unprecedented; separately NOS reports Albert Heijn, Etos and Gall &amp; Gall in the Netherlands took websites down after a Sunday-afternoon cybersecurity incident with Belgium's Delhaize (also Ahold Delhaize) also disrupted; early losses approaching 300k euros, potentially several million nationwide (primary tomshardware.com/tech-industry/cyber-security/unprecedented-cyberattack-cripples-supermarket-fridges-across-europe-as-hackers-activate-automatic-defrosting-delivery-and-store-prices-also-impacted-by-incident verified via direct curl --http1.1 -4 page fetch at ~12:25 UTC Oct 12, 2007199 bytes, datePublished 2026-10-12T11:32:54+00:00, byline Stephen Warwick, citing La Dépêche and the Coop U president's X confirmation; ladepêche.fr and nos.nl not probed this session, so the verified Tom's Hardware disclosure is cited per the relay precedents). New territory - grep shows zero prior supermarket/Danfoss/refrigeration entries (<a data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046/hovercard" href="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046"><tt>ebdaf93</tt></a> recorded the related Ahold-Delhaize supermarket cybersecurity-incident newsroom statement 10:41:55Z as a corporate-PR skip - Ahold Delhaize is Albert Heijn's parent, the same arc's earlier Dutch signal). Categorized 后端 per the security-campaign precedents (CyberXero, Bricksforge, CISA KEV). (2) QGIS merged QEP428 "No AI contributions permitted" (PR #387 authored by core contributor Nyall Dawson): the proposal replaces the project's earlier QEP-408 AI tool policy (Even Rouault's human-in-the-loop policy adapted from LLVM's AI Tool Use Policy, which required reviewing all LLM output, transparency via Assisted-by trailers, and banned unreviewed agent comments) with a total ban - "No LLM, AI or agent assisted code contributions are allowed in the qgis/qgis repository. If we subsequently discover that you have used an AI, LLM, or any agent-based workflow for your contribution, you will be subject to code reversion and contributor rights sanctioning"; in the PR discussion Dawson said the intent is to start with a closed door and selectively open it case-by-case later (e.g. AI as autocomplete replacement, translations), that the earlier policy's process clearly didn't happen in reality, and that the project had already lost at least one extremely high value contributor as a result; the QEP passed its discussion period Oct 5, moved to voting, and was merged into QGIS-Enhancement-Proposals master Oct 7 (primary github.com/<a data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5565065750" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/qgis/QGIS-Enhancement-Proposals/issues/387" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/qgis/QGIS-Enhancement-Proposals/pull/387/hovercard" href="https://github.com/qgis/QGIS-Enhancement-Proposals/pull/387">qgis/QGIS-Enhancement-Proposals/pull/387</a> verified via direct curl --http1.1 -4 page fetch at ~12:30 UTC Oct 12, 634350 bytes, page title "Add QEP428: No ai contributions permitted by nyalldawson · Pull Request #387", plus the PR .diff fetch (160 lines) carrying the full replacement policy text; api.github.com unreachable this session so the HTML page and .diff served as verification). Gap-fill disclosure: the merge sits Oct 7, inside the 14-day window, but no feed in the standing 45 set carries QGIS QEP activity and no commit message records it; the 79-point HN submission 2026-10-12T11:22:24Z is the first in-set visibility, per the HashiCorp-Boundary/DuckDB/Genkit/AISI/Mistral gap-fill precedents; entry dated by discovery time per the AISI precedent (2026-10-12 11:22). New territory - grep shows zero prior QGIS entries. Categorized AI per the AI-coding-governance substance. (3) Alibaba Qwen released QwenGyre, an online reinforcement learning framework for long-horizon agent tasks (relay ithome.com/1/012/066.htm verified via direct curl --http1.1 -4 page fetch at ~12:28 UTC Oct 12, 24251 bytes, page stamp 2026/10/12 19:20:43 Beijing = 11:20:43Z matching the ithome feed stamp exactly, byline 潞源): agent runs routinely stretch to hours with hundreds of interdependent model-environment interactions and millions of cumulative tokens; QwenGyre splits GPUs into compute units so units freed by finished batch tasks roll into training while running tasks keep their state and caches intact without restart; Token-in Token-out records the true context of every output segment, organizes trajectories into a tree by shared prefix and expands only the selected path into training samples; Partial Scoring yields usable feedback for timed-out but partially-complete tasks; official NL2RepoBench online RL experiments with ~700k-token rollouts lifted pass rate from 52.5% to 58.5% over 48 training steps with a 1.78x end-to-end speedup vs Async at equal GPU budget, and cross-task validation on Qwen3.6-122B covered NL2RepoBench/DeepSWE/TerminalBench; qwenlm.github.io blog and github.com both unreachable this session (curl exit 28 under the continuing flaky route) so no primary could be probed and the verified ithome relay is cited per the Reuters/Korea Herald relay precedents. New territory - grep shows zero prior QwenGyre entries. Categorized AI per the framework-release precedents. Evaluated and skipped: HN sweep (hn.algolia search_by_date with numericFilters created_at_i &gt; 1791803100 - this cutoff is 11:05:00Z real UTC Oct 12, five minutes before <a data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046/hovercard" href="https://github.com/xizhou0606/ai-interview-experience/commit/ebdaf93d24907e2c7eed6bc93eaf606a5b2e5046"><tt>ebdaf93</tt></a>'s stated 11:10 coverage end per the standing sweep-cutoff convention): clean single-page pull, 61 hits spanning 11:08:10Z-12:19:04Z with 0 cutoff violations; the pre-11:10 overlap hits (Show-HN http-server-rs 11:08:10Z, NYT book-freezer 11:09:18Z) and all new hits evaluated - skipped: Ledger unauthorized-hardware-implant