        </p>
      </div>
    
        
      

      
        <figcaption data-sqsp-image-classic-block-caption-container="">
          <p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">An  example above of the kind of misinformation spreading low-lifes that infest Reddit and LinkedIn.</p>
        </figcaption>
      
    
      </figure>
    

    


  </div><div data-sqsp-text-block-content="" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/45a223c2-0a7f-41e1-910b-7e4ed1931d30_973/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="yui_3_17_2_1_1791644064165_3042" id="block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791644064165_3042"><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">We should clear the air here. Subscription software exists when cloud services and cloud compute are integrated into a software suite. It is the only way to pay for the running costs at wide scale. If you remove these modern services there is limited progress in software development. You'll have to move all high cost compute locally which is impractical because most users cannot afford a high end workstation GPU or cloud server.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Instead of hurling hate speech and bile at thousands of software engineers who lead innovation at large companies (Adobe, Autodesk, Maxxon, Celsys, and others), show them some gratitude for their efforts. They are the engineers who innovate and everyone else follows. Just because they work at a big company doesn't mean they are committing human rights abuses. We have a generation brainwashed by envy and hate instead of urging everyone to be greater and bigger.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">If some people have an issue with companies being large, they now have the tools to compete against them. But instead of vibe cloning poor quality rip offs why not build new original creative applications around fresh ideas that have never been tried before?</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">But then again, vibe cloned piracy is a demotivating force. It ruins the incentive to create. Why create new original apps and games if someone comes along and rips you off?</p></div><div data-test="image-block-inline-outer-wrapper" data-sqsp-image-classic-block-layout="inline" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.imageLayout/5f2441fc-5dad-41e4-95d7-d4af4d2e4d6f_217/website.components.imageLayout.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.imageLayout/5f2441fc-5dad-41e4-95d7-d4af4d2e4d6f_217/website.components.imageLayout.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.imageLayout" data-sqsp-block="image-classic" data-website-component-id="yui_3_17_2_1_1791644432193_3559" id="block-yui_3_17_2_1_1791644432193_3559">

    

    

    
